  "title": "External Balance Check in WERC7575ShareToken::unregisterVault Enables Vault Registry Denial-of-Service",
  "body": "## Summary\nThe `unregisterVault()` function in `WERC7575ShareToken` can be permanently blocked by sending 1 wei of the underlying asset directly to the vault address. Combined with the `MAX_VAULTS_PER_SHARE_TOKEN = 10` limit, this allows an attacker to fill all registry slots and then \"dust\" each vault, permanently locking the vault registry.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `unregisterVault()` function enforces a strict balance check:\n\n```solidity\ntry ERC20(asset).balanceOf(vaultAddress) returns (uint256 vaultBalance) {\n    if (vaultBalance != 0) revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n}\n```\n\nThis check uses `balanceOf()` (external balance) rather than internal accounting (`totalAssets()`). Neither `WERC7575Vault` nor `ERC7575VaultUpgradeable` implements a `sweep()` function to remove excess tokens not backed by shares.\n\n### Attack Vector\n\n1. Attacker sends 1 wei of the underlying asset directly to the vault contract address\n2. Admin attempts to call `unregisterVault()`\n3. Transaction reverts with `CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance()` because `balanceOf(vault) == 1`\n4. Vault remains registered indefinitely\n\n### Registry Lockout Scenario\n\n````\n1. Admin registers 10 vaults (max capacity)\n2. Registry: 10/10 slots filled\n3. Attacker sends 1 wei to each vault address (cost: ~10 wei + gas)\n4. All vaults are now \"dusted\"\n5. Admin cannot unregister any vault (all fail balance check)\n6. Admin cannot register new vaults (at max capacity)\n7. Result: Registry permanently locked\n````\n\n## Recommended Mitigations\nReplace `balanceOf()` with `totalAssets()` which tracks internal accounting:\n\n```diff\n- try ERC20(asset).balanceOf(vaultAddress) returns (uint256 vaultBalance) {\n-    if (vaultBalance != 0) revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n}\n\n+ uint256 internalBalance = IERC4626(vaultAddress).totalAssets();\n+ if (internalBalance != 0) revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n```\n\nor you can add a function to remove dust from vaults:\n\n```solidity\nfunction sweep(address token, uint256 amount) external onlyOwner {\n    uint256 excess = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this)) - totalAssets();\n    require(amount <= excess, \"Cannot sweep user funds\");\n    IERC20(token).transfer(msg.sender, amount);\n}",
